SoftLadder
==========

Copyright 2025 Jorge Viloria

SoftLadder is a clean-room, from-scratch reimplementation of the ideas and
file-format conventions of ClassicLadder in Rust. It is licensed to the public
under the terms of the MIT license or the Apache License, Version 2.0, at your
option (see LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE).

Prior art acknowledgement
-------------------------

ClassicLadder
  A ladder-logic PLC editor and runtime originally written in C by
  Marc Le Douarain and contributors.
  Project home: https://github.com/MaVaTi56/classicladder
  License: GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL) v2.1 or later.

  SoftLadder reuses the *ideas* of ClassicLadder: its programming model, the
  `%`-notation for variable references, the naming of ladder elements and the
  layout of the text project container. No ClassicLadder source code has been
  copied, translated, ported or otherwise incorporated into SoftLadder.

Clean-room statement
--------------------

This project is a clean-room reimplementation. Its implementation was written
from the published behaviour and documentation of ClassicLadder, and from the
on-disk file formats that ClassicLadder reads and writes, without copying or
mechanically translating any C source code. Consequently SoftLadder is not a
derivative work of ClassicLadder and is distributed under the permissive
licenses named above rather than under the LGPL.

Users migrating from ClassicLadder remain responsible for the licensing of
their own project files and of the ClassicLadder build they migrate from.
